    "name": {
      "cards": [
        {
          "text": "Music names its notes with seven letters: A, B, C, D, E, F, G. That is the [[musical-alphabet|musical alphabet]], and each letter is a [[note-name|note name]].",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "A3",
              "B3",
              "C4",
              "D4",
              "E4",
              "F4",
              "G4"
            ],
            "low": "A3",
            "high": "G4"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "After G the alphabet starts again at A. So a keyboard has many As and many Gs. The gap from one A to the next A is an [[octave|octave]]: the same name, but higher or lower.",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "A3",
              "A4"
            ],
            "low": "A3",
            "high": "A4"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "These seven letters name the white keys. The black keys get their names in Grade 1. To find a letter, start at C, which you can spot by the twos, and count along.",
          "exhibit": {
            "kind": "keyboard",
            "highlight": [
              "C4",
              "D4",
              "E4",
              "F4",
              "G4"
            ],
            "low": "C4",
            "high": "B4"
          }
        }
      ],
      "alternative": {
        "text": "Think of the days of the week. After Sunday comes Monday again, so nobody runs out of days. The keyboard does the same with letters. After G, it goes back to A, and the cycle carries on up the keys."
      }
    },
